## Summary

Data quality on the board is clean (board-health reports 0 missing fields; Tier 1/2 analytics complete), so I took the recommended fallback and fixed a real tooling defect in **`dedup-detector.js`**.

**The bug:** The detector was flagging the three future quarterly Texas sales-tax tasks (Q4 2026 / Q1 2027 / Q2 2027, plus the done Q3) as a duplicate cluster at 0.8 similarity — every single run. They're legitimately distinct recurring instances, so this was a standing false positive that wasted review cycles.

**The fix:** Added `periodSignature()` (extracts quarter/year/month markers from a title) and `periodsDiffer()`. When two titles are highly similar but carry *different* period markers, they're treated as distinct recurring instances and skipped. Verified:
